      "id": "clm_01M4VEBZBYT7FESJJKRP20C7XJ",
      "statement": "The foundation of the Second Temple was laid in the second year after the return under Cyrus (c. 536/535 BC), before the work stopped until 520.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Ezra.3.8",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Ezra 3:8 with 4:24 and 5:16 supports an early foundation; Keil (535/534) and Ryle (536) defend it, Ryle answering three objections. Batten places the foundation in 520 on the basis of Haggai and Zechariah and regards Ezra 3:6b–4:3 as a displaced parallel; 1 Esdras and Josephus place the scene in Darius's reign; Kosters (reported by both) rejected it as unhistorical. No external evidence dates the foundation.",
